From 406b59b0a020141aca703ed05e3d58685069b461 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:25:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Map msgbuf packet IDs bidirectionally

Since commit f0ba5fd51ff2 ("wifi: brcmfmac: Set DMA direction for msgbuf
packet IDs") the TX and RX packet ID pools really use DMA_TO_DEVICE and
DMA_FROM_DEVICE, where they previously, by accident, used
DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL. On Apple's BCM4388 (M4 MacBook Air and Mac mini,
firmware 23.50.20.2) the firmware accesses these buffers in both
directions: with TX mapped device-read-only through the PCIe DART it
reports "H2D DMA data transfer error" right after the first LINK event
and traps, and with only TX widened it still dies as soon as association
starts. Every later dcmd then times out and Wi-Fi never associates.
Bisected on the Air by asahi-03: with both pools bidirectional the 7.3
kernel joins again, with TX alone it does not.

Map both packet ID pools bidirectionally again, as before f0ba5fd51ff2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Original-Commit: 9188e149997d90434767ea162a5bf2b35f655ce1
Signed-off-by: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Assisted-By: LLM
---
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
index 659419e017c5..39eb24ec6406 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -1719,12 +1719,19 @@ int brcmf_proto_msgbuf_attach(struct brcmf_pub *drvr)
 	msgbuf->max_ioctlrespbuf = BRCMF_MSGBUF_MAX_IOCTLRESPBUF_POST;
 	msgbuf->max_eventbuf = BRCMF_MSGBUF_MAX_EVENTBUF_POST;
 
+	/*
+	 * Packet buffers stay mapped bidirectionally, as they effectively were
+	 * before the direction was stored. The BCM4388 firmware accesses
+	 * both pools in both directions: with TX device-read-only it traps
+	 * with "H2D DMA data transfer error", and with only TX widened it
+	 * still dies once association starts.
+	 */
 	msgbuf->tx_pktids = brcmf_msgbuf_init_pktids(NR_TX_PKTIDS,
-						     DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+						     DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 	if (!msgbuf->tx_pktids)
 		goto fail;
 	msgbuf->rx_pktids = brcmf_msgbuf_init_pktids(NR_RX_PKTIDS,
-						     DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
+						     DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
 	if (!msgbuf->rx_pktids)
 		goto fail;
 
-- 
